1
00:07:53,333 --> 00:07:59,333
Some of the greatest battles are fought with the heart.

2
00:15:46,666 --> 00:15:52,666
Lady Jane is a drama, romance, history film directed by Trevor Nunn.

3
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:46,000
The death of King Henry VIII throws his kingdom into
chaos because of succession disputes.

4
00:31:33,333 --> 00:31:39,333
His weak son, Edward, is on his deathbed.

5
00:39:26,666 --> 00:39:32,666
Anxious to keep England true to the Reformation, a scheming minister John Dudley marries off his
son, Guildford to Lady Jane Grey, whom he places on the throne after Edward dies.

6
00:47:20,000 --> 00:47:26,000
At first hostile to each other, Guildford and Jane fall in love, but they cannot
withstand the course of power which will lead to their ultimate downfall.

7
00:55:13,333 --> 00:55:19,333
Lady Jane Grey, played by Helena Bonham Carter.

8
01:03:06,666 --> 01:03:12,666
Guilford Dudley, played by Cary Elwes.

9
01:11:00,000 --> 01:11:06,000
John Dudley, Duke of Nothumberland, played by John Wood.

10
01:18:53,333 --> 01:18:59,333
Henry Grey, Duke of Suffolk, played by Patrick Stewart.

11
01:26:46,666 --> 01:26:52,666
Sir John Bridges, played by Joss Ackland.

12
01:34:40,000 --> 01:34:46,000
Dr. Feckenham, played by Michael Hordern.

13
01:42:33,333 --> 01:42:39,333
Lady Jane is a 1986 British costume-historical drama romance film, directed by Trevor Nunn,
written by David Edgar, and starring Helena Bonham Carter as the title character.

14
01:50:26,666 --> 01:50:32,666
It tells the story of Lady Jane Grey, her marriage to Lord Guildford Dudley, and her
reign as the "Nine Days' Queen" following the death of Edward VI of England.

15
01:58:20,000 --> 01:58:26,000
The story had previously been turned into a 1936 film, Tudor Rose, and a
1923 silent film, Lady Jane Grey; Or, The Court of Intrigue.

16
02:06:13,333 --> 02:06:19,333
The film explores themes of tudor, tuberculosis, 16th century, british monarchy.

17
02:14:06,666 --> 02:14:12,666
The tone is emotional.
